@ohiain I totally agree - if you just focus on showing up and for yourself, the time adds up. The best comparison is with your own past self (me vs 2025 me during a bull run, me vs 2025 me in a choppy tape etc). 

I think it’s healthy to be aspirational for sure - there will always be someone leagues ahead of you. It’s just that as you grow, those aspirations graduate as well. 

You mentally anchor to other successful people who are leagues ahead of you in your present state. By next year you might be close to what you aspired for this year and so on.. Overall, having a positive attitude about everything helps a lot along the way. Just have a ball, have fun along the way. What is life if not lived to the fullest..

